4-602.13 The following were observed to be soiled:
1. Wire shelving unit holding panini presses - top shelf (old bread ties with buildup of crumbs) & bottom shelf (grease/dust buildup);
2. General outer surfaces of panini presses and trays underneath (food debris); 
3. Bottom inside reach-in freezer under the pizza ovens (food crumbs);
4. Bottom inside pizza prep cooler (food crumbs/splash); 
5. General surfaces of dish machine (general buildup); 
6. Sides of cooking equipment and coolers (grease/general buildup); 
7. Spice storage containers and shelving next to bulk flour in dry storage (powder accumulation); and
8. Bulk flour roll cart (powder accumulation).
Cleaning frequency was discussed. 
Nonfood contact surfaces shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to eliminate buildup of grease, food splash and general debris.
